# Build-context exclusions for `docker/api.Dockerfile` and `docker/worker.Dockerfile`.
#
# Both images install the project **editable** (`pip install -e .`), so the source tree is
# copied into the image rather than compiled into a wheel. That is not a shortcut: the
# `[tool.setuptools.package-data]` block in `pyproject.toml` declares only
# `app/config/*.yaml`, so a wheel would silently omit `app/ai/prompts/*.md` and
# `app/documents/templates/*.j2` — the prompts and the resume templates. The image would
# build, start, and then fail at the first tailoring pass with a missing-prompt error.
#
# Because the whole tree is copied, this file is what keeps the context small and keeps
# host state out of the image. Two categories matter most:
#
#   * secrets — `.env` carries real API keys, and a copied-in `.env` would override every
#     value compose sets, silently, with whatever the developer had locally;
#   * host-specific build output — `desktop/src-tauri/target/` and `node_modules/` are
#     gigabytes of artefacts compiled for the host, useless to a Linux container.

# ── Version control and CI ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# ── Secrets and local environment ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `.env.example` is deliberately NOT excluded: it is the documented template and carries no
# credential. Every real `.env*` is.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets.json
.credentials/

# ── Python build / test / tool state ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
*.egg
.eggs/
build/
dist/
sdist/
wheels/
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
.tox/
.nox/
.hypothesis/

# ── Runtime state (recreated inside the container under DATA_DIR) ──────────────────────
var/
/storage/
/cache/
screenshots/
traces/
browser-profile/
*.har
*.trace.zip
.applicantos/
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db-journal
logs/
*.log

# ── The desktop app ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A Tauri application is not containerised (see docs/PACKAGING.md). None of it is needed by
# the API or the worker, and `src-tauri/target` alone is several gigabytes.
desktop/

# ── Docker's own files ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Dockerfiles are passed with `-f`; nothing inside the image reads them, and excluding
# them keeps an edit to a compose file from invalidating the source layer.
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.override.yml
docker-compose.*.yml
docker/grafana/
docker/prometheus/

# ── Editor and OS noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.claude/
